METHOD
For each length from one through 1000, the audit constructs the exact
unperiodized line kernel

  W_hat=tau_1^length,
  tau_1(z)=z^(-2)+2z^(-1)+3+2z+z^2,

using arbitrary-precision integers.  At half-level K=2 and period L=6
it checks every individual paired-slope summand

  b_(jL+r)+b_((j+1)L-r-2),
  b_t=delta_hat(t)-delta_hat(t+1),
  delta_hat(t)=W_hat(t)-W_hat(t+1),

and every coordinate and adjacent monotonicity margin of every proper
outside-in suffix D_n.

The first negative paired-slope summand occurs exactly at length 57,
image j=1, and label r=0.  Hence termwise paired-slope positivity is
false even for an actual all-Q=1 factor word.  Its complete D_1 suffix,
printed on the same line, is nevertheless positive and strictly
decreasing.  The scan finds 6,181 negative individual summands but no
negative suffix coordinate and no suffix-monotonicity failure through
length 1000.  The latter zero counts are bounded evidence for the
global suffix inequality, not an unbounded proof.

At K=2 the audit also evaluates at every active affine wall nL the
exact generator payment

  m_4+m_5+m_6+m_7-2u_1-2u_2

with all indices translated by nL-L.  All 166,833 values are
nonnegative.  Thus the all-wall AIMGP hierarchy
survives the same long-word regime which disproves termwise
paired-slope positivity.  This is bounded evidence, not a proof.

